    "abstract": "Illustrated parts figure for the forward lower shell skin panels and the longitudinal lap joint between stations 1080 and 1360, split over two sheets so that the delivered joint configuration and the re-sealed one can be ordered from separately.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the skin panel details, the lap joint splice parts and the external doubler strap of the forward lower shell between stations 1080 and 1360, on the left and the right side of the aircraft.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the joint at the pre-modification standard with the aft splice plate visible; sheet 2 shows the same area with the external bonded strap installed, and the strap footprint hides items 30 and 40 on that sheet. The second sheet was raised as a part list change against the interfay sealing improvement, so that a station can order for either configuration without reading the effectivity of every item on one drawing. The figure is drawn for the left side; the right side is a mirror image with the same part numbers except for the handed clip at item 50. Fastener quantities are given for one side only. Items marked as an alternate carry the effectivity that applies to their build standard and must not be mixed on one joint."
    },
